{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Honor your father.</b> Here He added 'and that it may go well with you' (ולמען ייטב לך), to say that his days will be good — and this is the reward of the commandment in its fruits in this world. And this addition with the letter ת I have already explained in the section of Yitro. And the vav-conjunction (הווי״ן) in the commandments of the second tablet, by way of the plain sense (peshat), is because this is a narration of matters by Moses of what had already occurred, and therefore the vav-conjunctions appear in the narration of his words, after the custom of men in the third person." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah,</b> the addition of the vav-conjunctions alludes that 'keep' (שמור), which is the ה״א, is included in the וא״ו; and likewise (Psalms 62:12) 'One thing has Elohim spoken, two have I heard' (אחת דבר אלהים שתים זו שמעתי). And He did not mention 'You shall not murder,' because its matter is judgment (דין), and the וא״ו is mercy (רחמים); and since He mentioned 'You shall not murder,' it was necessary to add 'and you shall not covet' in order to complete the five prohibitions with vav-conjunctions, corresponding to the final ה״א which includes the letter וא״ו. And observe that 'a great voice' (קול גדול) 'and it did not continue' (ולא יסף) — that is the וא״ו; for the word 'voice' (קול) is joined to 'great' (גדול), while 'the sound of words you hear' (קול דברים אתם שומעים) is the ה״א; and the sense of 'and it did not continue' (ולא יסף) is that He did not add to the voice you heard to cause it to be heard by you ever again — and this teaches you that the congregation never attained it, but attained only the ה״א alone; and this is what it says: 'no form you saw' (ותמונה אינכם רואים), that is, even the form (ותמונה) written concerning Moses (Numbers 12:8): 'and the form of HaShem he beholds' (ותמונת ה׳ יביט) — you do not see, that is, do not attain; aside from this voice, that is, this 'sound of words.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:55.195046099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}